# Fixture for `just diagnostic-stream-smoke`: an `if` with no `else`.
#
# Parse errors surface through the BUNDLER, not the checker, so they take a
# different reporting path than unknown_variable.spr and need their own fixture:
# `ERROR: bundle: ...` vs `ERROR: check: ...`. Covering only one path would leave
# the other free to regress.
#
# WHY THIS SHAPE. The obvious probe — a malformed parameter list, `fn main( -> Unit`
# — is not FORMATTER-STABLE: `fmt_bin` rewrites it to `fn main(-> Unit` and repo-wide
# `just fmt-check` then fails on the fixture itself. A missing `else` is a parse error
# the token-based formatter leaves untouched, which is why the existing
# tests/conformance/parse_error/missing_else.spr uses it too.
#
# Expected: `ERROR: bundle:` on stderr, nonzero exit.
fn unreachable(x: Int) -> Int =
  if x > 0 then 1
